# Config-driven content (required)

**Default rule:** If copy, branding, nav, colors, feature toggles, or homepage content can reasonably live in
config — it must. Code changes should not be required to rebrand or rewrite marketing text.

## Where content lives

| Kind                                        | Location                                                            |
| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Per-gym brand, theme, nav, labels, features | `src/config/gyms/<slug>.ts`                                         |
| Shared defaults                             | `src/config/base.ts`                                                |
| Resolver / merge                            | `src/config/index.ts` — `getGymConfig()`, `mergeHomepageSections()` |
| Admin live overrides                        | Supabase `gym_page_sections` (overlays file defaults)               |
| Types                                       | `src/config/types.ts`                                               |

## Do

- Read config via `getGymConfig()` (or slug argument) in Server Components
- Pass `GymConfig` (or slices) into presentational components as props
- Add new gyms by **new config file + registry entry**, not forked components
- Use `labels.*` for button/link text (`prSubmit`, `leaderboard`, …)
- Use `features.*` to gate modules (`socialFeed`, `competitions`, …)
- Use `homepageSections[]` with typed `type` + `props` for public homepage blocks
- Keep Iron Asylum / gym-specific strings **only** in config/seed SQL

## Do not

- Hardcode gym names, taglines, phone, address, or hours in `src/components/` or `src/app/`
- Duplicate theme hex values in components — use `themeToCssVars(config)` / CSS variables
- Add one-off marketing strings in JSX when they belong in section `props` or `labels`

## Adding new UI surface area

1. Extend types in `src/config/types.ts` if needed
2. Add defaults to `base.ts` or gym config
3. Build a **reusable** component that accepts props/config
4. Wire admin editor to persist overrides when staff should edit without deploy

## Example

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
const config = getGymConfig();
<h1>{config.labels.leaderboard}</h1>

// ❌ BAD
<h1>Leaderboards</h1>
```
